        <body>
            <div xml:id="d186">

                <pb facs="0341" n="279" sameAs="frus:frus1878/pg279"/>

                <head>No. 181.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Welsh to Mr. Evarts</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1878-07-02"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 2, 1878</date>.
                        (Received July 13.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 104.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my dispatch, No. 98, of the
                    22d ultimo, I have the honor to acquaint you that I received yesterday, from Mr.
                    Cross, a reply to the note which I addressed to him on the 18th of June on the
                    subject of the invitation to Great Britain to join the bi-metallic
                    conference.</p>
                <p>I telegraphed to you yesterday, by cable, the substance of Mr. Cross’s
                    communication, and I inclose herewith a copy of the same <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >in extenso</hi>.</p>
                <p>I have received a communication from Mr. Hitt, chargé d’affaires <hi
                        rendition="#italic">ad interim</hi> in Paris, stating that he was authorized
                    to announce that it had been suggested that the day for the meeting of the
                    conference should be postponed to the tenth day of August, and I have acquainted
                    Mr. Cross with the proposed change of date.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN WELSH.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d186-a1.xml" xpointer="d186-a1"/>
            </div>
